            <ArticleTitle>Polyetherketoneketone (PEKK), a framework material for complete fixed and removable dental prostheses: A clinical report.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0022-3913(17)30636-4</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.prosdent.2017.09.008</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This clinical report demonstrates the use of polyetherketoneketone (PEKK) as a framework material with individually luted heat-pressed lithium disilicate glass-ceramic crowns for an implant-supported complete fixed dental prosthesis (ICFDP) and a conventional complete removable dental prosthesis (CRDP). This prosthesis design provides a non-computer-aided design and computer-aided manufacturing (CAD-CAM) option for the fabrication of ICFDPs and CRDPs with individualized ceramic crowns for optimal esthetics. The performance of PEKK as a framework material needs to be assessed in clinical trials.</AbstractText>
